{
	"description": "Golden vectors for the previous/next desktop actions: macOS space_prev / space_next and space_prev_wrap / space_next_wrap, Windows and Linux desktop_prev / desktop_next and desktop_prev_wrap / desktop_next_wrap. Replayed by the macOS, Linux and Windows suites so the three drivers agree on where a step lands.",
	"rule": "index is the 0-based position of the current desktop among count desktops (count >= 1, 0 <= index < count). direction is prev or next. A step moves one position in that direction. At an edge a plain action (wrap false) stays where it is, and a wrapping action (wrap true) goes to the other end: next from the last desktop lands on the first, prev from the first lands on the last. With a single desktop both stay. target is the 0-based index the action lands on; target equal to index means no switch. The signed number of single steps is target - index.",
